Modifications:
--------------
This is a substantially modified version of Paraglidable, including:

1. Migration from TensorFlow 1.15 to TensorFlow 2.15+
   - Updated all deprecated tf.keras.backend.* APIs to modern TensorFlow 2.x equivalents
   - Refactored custom Keras layers for TF 2.x compatibility
   - Removed compute_output_shape() methods (automatic in TF2)
   - Updated model compilation and training code
   - New module structure: src/pyparaglide/models/

2. Python version requirement updated to Python 3.12+
   - Removed support for older Python versions
   - Updated all dependencies to modern versions

3. Architecture simplification
   - Removed Docker-based deployment
   - Removed Apache/PHP web server components
   - Removed C++/Qt5 tile generator
   - Converted to CLI-first application using Typer + Rich

4. Project structure modernization
   - Adopted src/ layout with pyproject.toml
   - Reorganized code into logical modules:
     * models/ - Neural network architecture (7 custom layers, 2 model types)
     * data/ - PKL data loading and normalization
     * training/ - Training logic with callbacks
     * config/ - Pydantic-based configuration
     * cli/ - Command-line interface
   - Added modern Python tooling (black, ruff, mypy, pytest)

5. Configuration management
   - Replaced environment detection with Pydantic Settings
   - Unified configuration through .env files with PYPARAGLIDE_ prefix

6. CLI commands implemented
   - pyparaglide version - Show version and dependency info
   - pyparaglide config - Display current configuration
   - pyparaglide info - System information
   - pyparaglide train - Train CELLS/SPOTS models
   - pyparaglide forecast - Generate flyability forecasts from GFS GRIB data

7. Forecast generation
   - Inference module for generating predictions
   - GribReader class for reading GFS GRIB2 files with pygrib
   - Forecaster class for running model predictions
   - JSON output format (no C++ tiler dependency)
   - Direct spot forecasts instead of map tiles

8. Data management
   - Downloads module: GFSDownloader for fetching GFS data from NOAA
   - Preprocessing module: DatasetBuilder for creating training PKL files
   - CLI commands: download, build-dataset
   - Parallel downloads with resume support
   - GRIB filtering to reduce storage needs

